Description: SEC: Avoid infinite loops for incomplete ASCII85 and ASCIIHex inline images
 A crafted/truncated inline image using the ASCII85Decode or ASCIIHexDecode
 filter can drive the extraction loops in pypdf.generic._image_inline into an
 infinite loop (denial of service). When end-of-stream is reached,
 read_non_whitespace() may still return a trailing byte while the following
 buffered read returns nothing, so the "not data_buffered" guard never fires
 and the loop keeps seeking back over the same bytes forever. Guard on the
 buffered read result (read_bytes) as well so the loop terminates and raises
 PdfReadError. Truncated inline-image settings (ContentStream._read_inline_image)
 are covered by CVE-2026-59936 (upstream PR #3891 / PdfStreamError).
CVE: CVE-2026-59935
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/commit/5a33a46416aa1ae6c025ff90a3cca57631fdafd2
