Description: SEC: Detect end of stream during inline image end marker detection
 An attacker can craft a PDF whose page content stream contains an unterminated
 inline image. While reading the inline-image settings dictionary in
 ContentStream._read_inline_image, end-of-stream makes read_non_whitespace()
 return empty bytes; the loop then seeks back and retries forever (DoS), e.g.
 during text extraction. Raise PdfStreamError when the token is empty so the
 loop terminates. Matches upstream ec3b145 / PR #3891 (CVE-2026-59936).
 Regression test lives in a standalone file to avoid colliding with
 GHSA-jm82-fx9c-mx94, which appends to tests/generic/test_data_structures.py.
